WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.022
Three ways.

2
00:00:01.182 --> 00:00:03.922
A textile is anything made of cloth or thread.

3
00:00:04.082 --> 00:00:06.404
You can make one by weaving, over and under.

4
00:00:06.564 --> 00:00:08.607
By stitching, in and out with a needle.

5
00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:13.179
Or by felting: rubbing wool with warm soapy water until it locks together.

6
00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:15.133
The running stitch.

7
00:00:15.293 --> 00:00:18.311
The running stitch is the first stitch most people learn.

8
00:00:18.471 --> 00:00:19.725
Tie a knot.

9
00:00:19.885 --> 00:00:21.232
Come up from the back.

10
00:00:21.392 --> 00:00:23.575
Go down a little way along, and up again.

11
00:00:23.735 --> 00:00:25.917
Use a big, blunt needle, with a grown-up.

12
00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:27.685
Choose the way.

13
00:00:27.845 --> 00:00:29.564
Each way is good at something.

14
00:00:29.724 --> 00:00:31.349
Weaving makes strong stripes.

15
00:00:31.509 --> 00:00:33.181
Stitching draws lines and names.

16
00:00:33.341 --> 00:00:35.524
Felting makes soft, round shapes.

17
00:00:35.684 --> 00:00:38.470
The same idea can often be made all three ways.

18
00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:40.006
Kantha.

19
00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:45.878
In Bengal, in Bangladesh and India, women stitch layers of old cloth together to make kantha.

20
00:00:46.038 --> 00:00:53.375
They stitch fish, flowers and birds, mostly with one simple stitch, running stitch, again and again.
